# Refactor cleanup

Canonical: `docs/Personal_Rules.md` section 3.

A leftover is the old path of a file this change moved, or a file this change left with no caller. Delete leftovers in the same piece of work; do not move them to a trash folder.

- Delete the old path and any folder the move left empty.
- Update or remove imports pointing at the old path.
- Delete a file whose last caller was removed in this change.
- Leave files already unused before this change; do not expand the task into a repository-wide unused-file purge.
- A missing import does not prove a file is unused. Routes, SQL scripts, wiki pages, tests, and configuration can be live without normal feature imports.
- A hold is a file/folder the owner explicitly said to keep. Record holds and reasons in `docs/Assumptions.md`; ask and wait before deleting one. No company hold list is inherited.
- Existing code is not automatically the target standard. Record routine choices in `Assumptions.md` and obtain agreement for architecture changes or exceptions.

Example: moving `TaskCard.tsx` into its feature folder also deletes its old path and a helper whose final caller was removed, while updating all imports.
